      "network": true,
      "caveats": "The tools never send anything. Each email, proposal or agreement goes out only after your own yes for that one message (as a Gmail draft you send, or through a Gmail MCP server you added), and the log steps refuse anything else. Two helpers go online with no login or keys: prospector/leads reads one public page per business website, slowly and identifying itself, and researcher/brief reads up to 4 public pages of one business. Cold email has to follow the law where you send it: in the US (CAN-SPAM) every email needs your postal address and a plain opt-out, which the opener's footer adds; in the UK, EU and Canada cold email to people needs a lawful basis or consent first. Anyone who says no goes on the suppression list and is never emailed again."
